摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Read-only GitHub access for agents, wrapping several tools. Inside the tool it automatically probes and selects whichever GitHub access method works locally, and tries network proxies on its own. That cuts down the network and parsing problems an agent may hit when accessing GitH","id":"gh:1339462797","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-github-router","slug":"AngelosZou/dsh-github-router","topics":["dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Read-only GitHub access for agents, wrapping several tools. Inside the tool it automatically probes "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"and selects whichever GitHub access method works locally, and tries network proxies on its own. That"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" cuts down the network and parsing problems an agent may hit when accessing GitH"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-github-router"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> Read-only GitHub access for a DeepSeek Harness project — load PRs, issues, files, and API data thr"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ough tools that route internally (API, gh CLI, git protocol, page HTML, mirrors), so an agent never "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"burns turns fighting shell-side TLS or proxy failures."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"A DeepSeek Harness plugin bundle that gives agents GitHub reads without shell retries:"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- **Five read-only tools** — `github_probe`, `github_pr`, `github_issue`, `github_file`, `github_api"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"` — plus the `github-router` skill and a system-prompt guidance section. No write, push, comment, or"},{"id":"p6s3","text":" mutation capability exists anywhere in the package.\n- **In-tool routing** — every request runs host"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"-side (outside the sandbox's TLS/proxy restrictions) and falls through a route ladder: `api.github.c"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"om` (direct → proxy) → `gh` CLI (read-only subcommands) → git protocol (plugin fetch cache, or a loc"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"al clone read with log/diff/show only) → PR/issue page HTML (strict JSON island extraction) → user-c"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"onfigured raw mirrors.\n- **One call, structured outcome** — PRs come back with metadata, discussion,"},{"id":"p6s8","text":" reviews, commits, changed files, and the diff, each part annotated with the route that served it; f"},{"id":"p6s9","text":"ailures return a route matrix instead of a dozen retried shell commands.\n- **Connectivity probe** — "},{"id":"p6s10","text":"`github_probe` reports which routes are live from the host in one call, with timings and a recommend"},{"id":"p6s11","text":"ed route chain.\n- **Zero runtime dependencies** — peers resolve from the DSH profile; proxied reques"},{"id":"p6s12","text":"ts travel through the plugin's own CONNECT tunnel (no third-party HTTP stack), so the package instal"},{"id":"p6s13","text":"ls fully offline.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- Node.js >= 22.19\n- Optional: the `gh` CLI (authenticated) for the gh route; `git` for the git rout"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" Node.js >= 22.19\n- Optional: the `gh` CLI (authenticated) for the gh route; `git` for the git route"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"From npm:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"From a local checkout (development):"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"From a git host:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Then **restart the DSH backend** — the host composition loads at process start. The tools appear in "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"new sessions: `github_probe`, `github_pr`, `github_issue`, `github_file`, `github_api`, plus the `gi"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ub_probe`, `github_pr`, `github_issue`, `github_file`, `github_api`, plus the `github-router` skill."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"This plugin tracks the DSH plugin API, which does not keep backward\ncompatibility between releases. "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"Pick the plugin version that matches your\nDeepSeek Harness release:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| DeepSeek Harness | Install |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| 0.1.7-rc.2       | `dsh-github-router@0.4.0` or later |\n| 0.1.2 ~ 0.1.6    | `dsh-github-router@0."},{"id":"p20s2","text":"3.2` |\n| 0.1.1 or earlier | `dsh-github-router@0.2.1` |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The mapping is recorded in `package.json` under `dsh.compatibility.dshReleases`."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Agent side:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| Tool | What it does |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| `github_probe` | One-shot connectivity matrix (api direct/proxy, gh installed/authed, git ls-remot"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"e, page direct/proxy, mirrors, token presence) with timings and a recommended route chain. Call firs"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"t when access fails or is slow. |\n| `github_pr` | Full PR view: metadata, description, discussion (i"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"ssue + inline review comments), reviews, commits, changed files, and the unified diff, each with rou"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"te attribution. Parts toggle (`includeDiscussion`/`includeReviews`/`includeCommits`/`includeFiles`/`"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"includeDiff`) and cap (`maxDiffBytes`/`maxItems`). `localRepo` (or session-cwd auto-detection) reads"},{"id":"p25s7","text":" commits/diff from a local clone with zero network. |\n| `github_issue` | Issue metadata, body, label"},{"id":"p25s8","text":"s, and comments, with route attribution. |\n| `github_file` | File content (or directory listing) at "},{"id":"p25s9","text":"a branch/tag/sha via api contents → raw → mirrors → git; returns size, truncation state, and the ser"},{"id":"p25s10","text":"ving route. |\n| `github_api` | Validated **GET-only** escape hatch for any `api.github.com` endpoint"},{"id":"p25s11","text":"; query values sanitized, responses cached, rate-limit headers surfaced, errors carry stable codes. "},{"id":"p25s12","text":" query values sanitized, responses cached, rate-limit headers surfaced, errors carry stable codes. |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Behavior notes:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- Route order is fixed per part type: API first (direct then proxy), then gh, then page HTML (proxy-"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"first — machines with reset direct TLS usually reach pages through the proxy), then git, then mirror"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"s. Each part records the route that served it.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- **Host-side execution** — plugin code runs in the host process, so the sandbox's TLS credential re"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"sets and proxy misrouting never apply. The unrestricted token is compensated by the confinement mode"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"l in SECURITY.md — not by weakening the sandbox.\n- **Explicit proxy decisions** — global `fetch` doe"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"s not inherit ambient proxy env; each attempt gets an explicit direct/proxy choice, and proxied requ"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"ests use a zero-dependency CONNECT tunnel (`node:http`/`node:tls`) with target-hostname TLS validati"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"on and `accept-encoding: identity`.\n- **Strict parsing** — the page-HTML route extracts only `react-"},{"id":"p30s7","text":"app.embeddedData` JSON islands and runs `JSON.parse` (never evaluated); a bounded BFS copies a white"},{"id":"p30s8","text":"list of fields, so CSRF tokens and the raw payload never reach the model.\n- **Argv-only subprocesses"},{"id":"p30s9","text":"** — every `gh`/`git` invocation is an argv array with fixed flag lists; user input reaches argv onl"},{"id":"p30s10","text":"y after regex validation, and nothing is shell-interpolated.\n- **Tool contract** — canonical values "},{"id":"p30s11","text":"are lossless JSON (arrays carry no side properties), byte-capped, and rendered as compact text with "},{"id":"p30s12","text":"route attribution.\n- **Skill & guidance** — the `github-router` skill teaches tool-first usage and t"},{"id":"p30s13","text":"he \"never escalate for GitHub reads\" rule; one system-prompt section (`dsh-github-router:guidance`, "},{"id":"p30s14","text":"order 118) reminds every session that the github_* tools are the sanctioned path."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Read-only by construction: no write verb exists, tokens attach only to\n`api.github.com` and are reda"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"cted on every boundary, page payloads are\nwhitelist-extracted, and the only disk writes are the two "},{"id":"p32s3","text":"plugin-owned\ncaches under `<DSH_HOME>/storages/dsh-github-router/`. See\nSECURITY.md for the complete"},{"id":"p32s4","text":" threat model and mitigation\nlist."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
